[IMPACT OF OUR WORK]

Implementation of audit recommendations is one of the critical enablers of efficient, effective and sustainable development. We started tracking implementation of recommendations made by Parliament on our reports, assessing the status of these recommendations by the Public Accounts Committee in its 2020/2021 Financial Year Report, adopted on 28 February,

2024 and the 24 th  Public Investments Committee report adopted on 7June, 2022. These reports seek to further improve on the follow-up of the implementation of recommendations by providing Parliament with an objective review on how the Accounting Officers have implemented the recommendations emanating from audit reports. The two reports findings are as listed;

[1. Status of implementation of recommendations of the 2020/2021 Public Accounts Committee]

We tracked five hundred and eighty (580) audit recommendations, across fifty-eight (58) entities and found that 79% of the recommendations had not been fully implemented.

